/-!
# Three movers, frozen readings [1, 2, 4]: the landing for ALL movers beyond the least frozen reading, in whichever lonely piece holds it (GENERATED by `s3cover_gen_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  Lonely pieces of the frozen set from `1/(8·1)` (exact), indexed from 0: [1/8, 7/32], [9/32, 7/16], [9/16, 23/32].
* `landL3124_<j>`: for ANY `d1, d2, d3 > 0`, IF no piece `i < j` holds a common clear instant of the three movers and piece `j` does, THEN the first lonely
  instant `T` of the frozen set with the three movers exists, lies in piece `j`, and is the first common clear instant at or after its left end.
  Earlier pieces are excluded by the hypothesis, the gaps by `fnot`, later pieces by order.
* `exists_union3_124`: for ALL real `d1, d2, d3 ≥ 1` some piece `j ≤ 2` holds a common clear instant (finite box cover of the sorted region `d1 ≤ d2 ≤ d3`: `1349` leaves;
  leaf kinds (kind, piece): {"('P', 0)": 166, "('P', 1)": 11, "('P', 2)": 1, "('R2', 0)": 680, "('R2', 1)": 86, "('R2', 2)": 8, "('R3', 0)": 294, "('R3', 1)": 93, "('R3', 2)": 10}; `d1 > 26` by `big3` in piece 1 [PROVISIONAL: counting tool]).
* `land3_later_124`: the assembled statement, no grid, no upper threshold.  No nonexistence of a common clear instant is proved for any box: the case split is on the
  statement itself (`by_cases` on each piece in turn).
Grades: [L]; the existence statement is discharged by a finite box cover [PROVISIONAL: covering]; `r2_rect`/`r3_rect`/`big3` are [PROVISIONAL: counting tool].
Not proved here: the cascade's path inside the piece; movers at or below `1`.
